-To address uneven sequencing effort, rarefaction aims to normalize metagenomic
-reads counts using repeated subsampling. The user first chooses the rarefaction
-depth and a number of iterations N. All the samples with metagenomic read counts
-below the specified depth are removed and then metagenomic reads are randomly
-drawn for the samples left to get subsampled reads at equal read depth.
-Then a beta diversity metric is calculated with the subsampled data and the
-process is iterated N times. Finally, beta diversity is estimated taking the mean
-of all beta diversity values calculated on subsampled data.
-
