-process is repeated a sufficient number of times, and if the rarefaction depth
-is set to the lowest metagenomic reads count found across all samples, no data
-will be omitted. Moreover, Patrick Schloss has demonstrated that rarefaction is
-"the only method that could control for variation in uneven sequencing effort
-when measuring commonly used alpha and beta diversity metrics" [@Schloss2023].
